# ==============================================================================
# Uncertainty-Weighted Experience Replay for Neural Contextual-Bandit
# Policy Learning
#
# Full revised simulation code
#
# Main methodological features
# ----------------------------
# 1. One-step contextual-bandit / potential-outcome framework.
# 2. No next-state transition and no conventional DQN TD target.
# 3. MLP is the primary architecture for static tabular states.
# 4. CNN-LSTM is retained as an architectural comparison using repeated
#    noisy measurements.
# 5. Replay strategies:
#       - Uniform
#       - Entropy Replay
#       - Residual-PER
#       - Quantum-Inspired Uncertainty Replay
# 6. Priority:
#
#       score_i(alpha) = 1 + alpha * U_i
#
#    Thus:
#
#       alpha = 0  ==> exactly uniform replay.
#
# 7. Importance-sampling correction:
#
#       w_i = (N_B p_i)^(-beta)
#
#    normalized by the largest weight.
# 8. Independent semisynthetic datasets for independent replications.
# 9. Same data/split across methods within each replication.
# 10. Train/validation/test split.
# 11. Alpha selected using validation data only.
# 12. Final test data used only for final evaluation.
# 13. Replication-level paired inference.
# 14. "Quantum-inspired" denotes a classical uncertainty heuristic.
# ==============================================================================


